---
import FirstRunTable from "../FirstRunTable.astro";
import Pipeline from "./Pipeline.astro";
import Voicemail from "./Voicemail.astro";
import { reported } from "../../lib/first-run";
import { bounds, story } from "../../lib/coverage";
import { noScore, pipeline, rileyAsk, spell } from "../../lib/cases";

const kickPlan = [
  `Download the schedule page from each of the ${spell(pipeline.asked)} school sites.`,
  "Parse each results table into rows: date, opponent, score.",
  "If a page fails, retry three times, log a warning, and continue so the run finishes.",
  "Read each match once, from the home team's page, so none counts twice.",
  "Compute played, goal difference and points, then sort and write the table.",
  "Print a summary: pages fetched, matches found, errors.",
];

const openings = [
  { gap: "How many matches to expect", kick: "Report the number found.", then: `${story.counted}, with nothing to compare it to.`, href: "#case-dunmore", where: "Case 1" },
  { gap: "Which page to read each match from", kick: "The host's page, once.", then: `One lost page removed ${spell(bounds.unseen)} matches and bent all ${spell(pipeline.rows)} rows.`, href: "#case-hartwell", where: "Case 2" },
  { gap: "What to do with a final that has no score", kick: "Leave the row out.", then: `${noScore.home} and ${noScore.away} are each one match short.`, href: "#case-cedar-grove", where: "Case 3" },
  { gap: "What to do when a site is silent", kick: "Retry three times, log a warning, carry on.", then: "The run finishes without Dunmore.", href: "#decision", where: "The decision" },
  { gap: "What the report must say", kick: "Pages fetched, matches found, errors.", then: "“All eight school sites, no errors.”", href: "#rewind", where: "Rewind" },
];

const choices = [
  ["stop", "Stop the run"],
  ["skip", "Skip it and carry on"],
  ["fill", "Fill in 0-0"],
  ["record", "Record the gap"],
];
---

<section id="setup">
  <h2>Setup: one sentence, one Friday</h2>
  <p>Here is the film's Friday again, slowly, as a problem with a cause.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>1</span>The ask</h3>
  <blockquote class="cv-ask">
    <p class="cv-who">Riley, to Kick <span>4:12</span></p>
    <p>{rileyAsk}</p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>It names the season, the sport, the sources and the product. It reads as complete.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>2</span>What Kick built</h3>
  <p>Kick built a scraper, a program that downloads pages made for people and pulls rows out of them.</p>
  <Pipeline />
  <details class="cv-more">
    <summary>Kick's plan, in its own words</summary>
    <ol class="cv-plan">{kickPlan.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ol>
  </details>
  <p>A pipeline can be asked three questions.</p>
  <ul class="cv-three">
    <li class="is-here"><b>Is everything here?</b><span><strong>Completeness.</strong> This module.</span></li>
    <li><b>Is each value in a usable form?</b><span>Cleansing. <a href="../04-parsing/">Modules 4</a> and <a href="../05-identity/">5</a>.</span></li>
    <li><b>Does each record obey the rules?</b><span>Validation. <a href="../06-contracts/">Modules 6</a> and <a href="../07-gates/">7</a>.</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>All {story.counted} of Kick's matches are real and correctly read, so cleansing and validation would both pass this table. A missing record has nothing to fail.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>3</span>What the ask left open</h3>
  <p>Kick filled five openings in the sentence with reasonable choices, and mentioned none. Open them one at a time.</p>
  <div class="cv-open">
    {openings.map((o) => (
      <details>
        <summary>{o.gap}</summary>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Kick chose</dt><dd>{o.kick}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Then</dt><dd>{o.then}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>See</dt><dd><a href={o.href}>{o.where}</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>4</span>What Riley saw</h3>
  <p>At 4:52 this was everything on Riley's screen.</p>
  <div class="cv-say">
    <p class="cv-who">Kick, the coding agent</p>
    <p>Done. All eight school sites, {story.counted} conference matches, no errors. Ready to publish.</p>
  </div>
  <FirstRunTable rows={reported} caption="The table Kick delivered" />
  <div class="cv-commit" data-commit>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-looks">What here looks wrong to you? Nothing is marked.</label>
    <textarea id="cv-looks" rows="2" data-save="looks-wrong"></textarea>
    <button type="button" disabled>Lock it in and read on</button>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write at least one sentence.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p>Eight rows, sorted, plausible numbers, no blanks. Dunmore on {spell(bounds.played)} played looks wrong only to someone who already knows the season is longer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>5</span>How it surfaced</h3>
  <p>Riley published at 4:58. The table's readers found the problem. Riley had no way to.</p>
  <div class="cv-calls">
    <Voicemail who="dolan" caller="Coach Dolan, Hartwell" time="5:41" line="We went into Dunmore October fifteenth and put seven on 'em. Seven-nothing. You've got us fourth." />
    <Voicemail who="dunmore" caller="Dunmore athletics" time="5:44" line="You've got our men at six conference games. We've played thirteen." />
    <Voicemail who="cedar" caller="Cedar Grove men's soccer" time="from the bus" line="September twenty-first, us and St. Lambert. That game happened. It's not in the standings." />
  </div>

  <h3 class="cv-step"><span>6</span>The problem, stated</h3>
  <p class="cv-lede">Kick's report described its program. Riley needed a report on the data. The records are clean and valid, and some are missing.</p>
  <div class="cv-say cv-yours" data-first hidden>
    <p class="cv-who">Your question from the film</p>
    <p data-first-text></p>
  </div>
  <fieldset class="cv-choice">
    <legend>Dunmore's site does not answer. What should Kick do?</legend>
    {choices.map(([value, label]) => (
      <label><input type="radio" name="cv-decision" value={value} data-save="decision" /><span>{label}</span></label>
    ))}
  </fieldset>
  <p class="cv-once">Nothing is marked. You come back to it in <a href="#decision">the decision</a>.</p>
  <p class="cv-can">Three cases follow, one per call. Then you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>say how many items a collection should hold, before it runs</li>
    <li>trace a gap to the block it removes, and bound what it touches</li>
    <li>tell empty, unknown and never asked apart</li>
    <li>choose what a collector does when a source is silent</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="cv-next">Start with the call that names the gap: Dunmore's.</p>
</section>
